WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:07.250
"Risks and Benefits of Red and Green Rooibos Tea"

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:09.600
Black, green, and white teas
are all made

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:11.840
from the same evergreen plant.

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:13.200
Herbal tea, on the other hand,

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:15.600
involves pouring water
over any plant in the world

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:17.640
other than the tea plant.

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:19.200
In my book How Not to Age,

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:21.320
I covered hibiscus
and chamomile tea

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:25.280
in my chapters on boosting AMPK
and blocking inflammation.

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:27.600
Are there any other
notable herbal teas

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:29.960
that may have
anti-aging properties?

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:32.920
Rooibos, also known as red tea,

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:34.360
is a caffeine-free herbal tea

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:36.840
grown in a mountainous region
of South Africa.

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:39.480
It has been shown to increase
the lifespan of C. elegans

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:41.000
by as much as 23 percent

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:43.320
under conditions
of oxidative stress,

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:46.240
presumed to be due
to its antioxidant properties.

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:49.280
In a head-to-head comparison
of fifteen herbal teas,

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:52.880
rooibos came in at number two
(after dandelion)

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:56.520
for in vitro
antioxidant power.

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:59.440
Green rooibos—
analogous to green tea—

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:01.480
worked better
in the C. elegans study

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:02.760
than red rooibos,

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:05.960
which is the commercially
more common oxidized form

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:07.560
(akin to black tea).

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:11.240
Green rooibos tea has about
twice the antioxidant capacity

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:12.480
compared to red,

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:15.880
though both similarly increase
the blood antioxidant capacity

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:17.480
after consumption.

00:01:17.480 --> 00:01:18.760
Within six weeks,

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:21.960
rooibos intake can decrease
markers of oxidative damage

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:25.600
and even drop LDL cholesterol
by nearly 27 points (mg/dl)

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:26.720
compared to control,

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:28.680
but the dose used
(six cups (1440 ml) a day)

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:30.640
is more than most people drink.

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:33.120
No smaller quantity
has apparently yet been

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:34.920
put to the test.

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:36.640
If you want to try it at home,

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:38.880
though the "optimal cup"
is said to require

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:40.080
10 minutes of steeping,

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:42.760
it appears extraction plateaus
at five minutes;

00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:45.480
so, more time
doesn't seem necessary.

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:47.080
The traditional
method of brewing

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:48.880
is to simmer the rooibos,

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:51.600
which does appear to improve
its antioxidant capacities

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:53.920
compared to
hot or cold steeping.

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:56.240
The practice fell into disfavor

00:01:56.240 --> 00:01:59.840
with the advent of tea bags
for convenience in the 1960s.

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:03.200
The same bag transition
happened to black tea—

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:05.960
jumping from 5 percent
in 1960 in the U.K.

00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:09.080
to more than 95 percent
by 2007—

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:11.520
but that switch
may have actually had

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:13.320
favorable consequences.

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:16.920
Because the tea in bags tends
to be chopped so much finer

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:18.280
than loose tea,

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:21.680
the extra surface area
improves the extraction.

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:23.640
It only takes two minutes
of infusion time

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:25.920
to extract the same quantity
of tea compounds

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:27.880
from bagged black tea

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:30.120
that it would take
ten minutes to extract

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:32.560
from loose leaf black tea.

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:36.240
Ideally, we should steep for
more than two minutes, though.

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:38.800
Flavonoid extraction
from black tea isn't complete

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:41.080
until about minute four.

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:42.960
Green tea maybe brewed
for three minutes

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:45.360
at 85 degrees C, Celsius

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:47.480
(for both optimum
nutrition and taste)

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:52.320
and white tea
at 98C for seven minutes.

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:55.520
(White tea brewed from bags
also results in almost twice

00:02:55.520 --> 00:02:59.200
the antioxidant capacity
of loose leaf.)

00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:02.280
Rooibos has
an excellent safety record,

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:04.200
though there have been
four cases reported

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:06.640
in the medical literature
of liver toxicity

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:08.640
associated with rooibos use,

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:10.280
the most convincing of which

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:12.360
involved two separate
hospitalizations

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:13.840
for acute hepatitis

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:17.520
following a resumption
of rooibos consumption.

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:19.520
All cases resolved
without incident

00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:22.240
once the patients stopped
drinking rooibos,

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:25.680
but as with any new tea,
herb, supplement, or drug,

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:29.000
immediately consult
your healthcare practitioner

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:31.560
if you develop
symptoms of liver trouble,

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:34.640
such as abdominal pain,
dark urine, or jaundice

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:37.400
(which is yellowing
of the skin or eyes).

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:41.280
One nice bonus to rooibos is
that it's effectively fair trade

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:42.240
by definition.

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:45.440
Starting in 1993, nearly
every country on the planet

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:48.280
ratified the Convention
on Biological Diversity,

00:03:48.280 --> 00:03:51.320
a breakthrough in global
environmental policymaking

00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:53.240
that aimed
to conserve biodiversity

00:03:53.240 --> 00:03:55.320
by rewarding Earth's custodians

00:03:55.320 --> 00:03:57.720
with fair and equitable
benefit sharing.

00:03:57.720 --> 00:03:59.760
And the rooibos
benefit sharing agreement

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:01.720
was the first
industry-wide agreement

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:03.560
to be formed
with indigenous peoples

00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:06.347
in accordance
with the Convention.

